{"nodes": [{"id": "neon_functions_skill", "label": "neon-functions Skill", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/neondatabase/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/neon-functions", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "neon_functions_skill_neon_function", "label": "Neon Function", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "# Neon Functions", "source_url": "https://github.com/neondatabase/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/neon-functions", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A long-running web-standard fetch handler on Node.js 24 deployed onto a branch, chosen over lambda-style serverless when the workload must outlast short execution caps and stay in the same region as its Postgres."}, {"id": "neon_functions_skill_runtime_limits", "label": "Timeouts and Runtime Limits", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Timeouts and Runtime Limits", "source_url": "https://github.com/neondatabase/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/neon-functions", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "15-minute time-to-first-byte, 15-minute silence heartbeat, and 15-minute waitUntil exist because Functions are a request/response runtime and not a background job runner; isolates are reused and evicted, so module state is per-isolate and in-memory only."}, {"id": "neon_functions_skill_module_scope_pool", "label": "Module-Scope pg Pool + attachDatabasePool", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Connecting to Postgres", "source_url": "https://github.com/neondatabase/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/neon-functions", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An isolate serves many requests, so a pool opened once at module scope amortizes connection setup and avoids exhausting Postgres; attachDatabasePool prevents node-postgres idle-client errors from becoming an uncaughtException that kills the isolate, and max is kept small because every isolate holds its own pool."}, {"id": "neon_functions_skill_function_env_vars", "label": "Injected Function Environment Variables", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Environment Variables", "source_url": "https://github.com/neondatabase/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/neon-functions", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "NEON_BRANCH, DATABASE_URL, DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED, auth and Data API URLs are injected at runtime; DATABASE_URL is left un-prefixed precisely because every ORM reads that name by default."}, {"id": "neon_functions_skill_agent_backend_direct_client", "label": "Client-Direct Agent Backend Pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Functions as an Agent Backend", "source_url": "https://github.com/neondatabase/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/neon-functions", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proxying the stream through a Vercel/Netlify route handler reimposes that host's ~10-60s cap, so the browser must call the Function directly with a short-lived JWT plus CORS; because the Function URL is public, the handler itself must verify the token or the agent is unauthenticated."}, {"id": "neon_functions_skill_websocket_server", "label": "WebSocket Server via upgradeWebSocket", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## WebSocket Servers", "source_url": "https://github.com/neondatabase/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/neon-functions", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The upgrade response must be returned unchanged because a 101 cannot be reconstructed as a plain Response; browsers cannot set WebSocket headers, so auth rides on a ?token= query param verified before upgrading."}, {"id": "neon_functions_skill_cross_isolate_fanout", "label": "Cross-Isolate Fan-Out Strategies", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "### Keeping clients in sync across isolates", "source_url": "https://github.com/neondatabase/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/neon-functions", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each isolate holds its own client set, and neon dev runs a single isolate, so in-process broadcast looks correct locally and silently fractures in production; polling Postgres is the default because it preserves Scale to Zero, LISTEN/NOTIFY needs always-on compute, and external pub/sub is for large fan-out."}, {"id": "neon_functions_skill_heartbeat", "label": "Stream Heartbeat", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "### Heartbeat (keep the socket alive)", "source_url": "https://github.com/neondatabase/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/neon-functions", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Neon's window is 15 minutes but intermediary proxies are far stricter, so a ~25s application-level keepalive is sent rather than relying on the app being chatty."}, {"id": "neon_functions_skill_sse_endpoint", "label": "SSE Endpoint on a Function", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Server-Sent Events (SSE)", "source_url": "https://github.com/neondatabase/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/neon-functions", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "For server-to-client-only streams SSE is simpler than a WebSocket \u2014 plain HTTP, no upgrade \u2014 and EventSource reconnects itself, so no client backoff has to be written."}, {"id": "neon_functions_skill_mcp_server", "label": "MCP Server on a Function", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## MCP Servers", "source_url": "https://github.com/neondatabase/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/neon-functions", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "MCP's streamable HTTP transport is a plain POST/GET on one endpoint, so it maps onto a fetch handler with no upgrade or extra protocol, and the tools read Postgres right next to the compute."}], "edges": [{"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_skill", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "metadata.parent: neon", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_functions_skill_neon_function", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill_runtime_limits", "target": "neon_functions_skill_neon_function", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Timeouts and Runtime Limits", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_functions_skill_module_scope_pool", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Connecting to Postgres", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_functions_skill_function_env_vars", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Environment Variables", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_functions_skill_agent_backend_direct_client", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Functions as an Agent Backend", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_functions_skill_websocket_server", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## WebSocket Servers", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_functions_skill_cross_isolate_fanout", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "### Keeping clients in sync across isolates", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_functions_skill_heartbeat", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "### Heartbeat", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_functions_skill_sse_endpoint", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Server-Sent Events (SSE)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_functions_skill_mcp_server", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## MCP Servers", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill_cross_isolate_fanout", "target": "neon_functions_skill_runtime_limits", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "several isolates in parallel, each with its own module state", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill_cross_isolate_fanout", "target": "neon_postgres_skill_scale_to_zero", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "polling preserves Scale to Zero; LISTEN/NOTIFY requires disabling it", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill_module_scope_pool", "target": "neon_functions_skill_function_env_vars", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill_neon_function", "target": "neon_skill_neon_ts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "preview.functions", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_skill_parse_env", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "parseEnv(config)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_ai_gateway_skill", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "point either at the Neon AI Gateway (see the `neon-ai-gateway` skill)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "neon_object_storage_skill", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "source_location": "see the neon-object-storage and neon-ai-gateway skills", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "neon_functions_skill", "target": "references_ai_sdk", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/neon-functions/SKILL.md", "sou